course: dictionary
lesson: 12212
title: Coniferous trees and forests
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a whole group of things, and coniferous is one of them. A coniferous tree has cones and needle-like or scaly leaves. Pine, fir, spruce and larch are all coniferous trees. «The coniferous trees stayed green all winter.» The word tells you what kind of tree is meant: one with cones.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Cones and needles help you picture the tree. «We walked through a coniferous forest of pine and fir.» Here coniferous describes the forest, which is made mainly of these trees. Ask yourself: what kind of tree or forest is being described?
explain: Coniferous is often compared with another word. «Deciduous trees lose their broad leaves in autumn, but coniferous trees keep their needles.» Coniferous and deciduous are opposite kinds of trees. Most coniferous trees stay green all year, while deciduous trees lose their leaves.
fact: Coniferous is an adjective. It describes a tree, a forest or a woodland.
fact: «Coniferous» means having cones and needle-like or scaly leaves.
fact: Most coniferous trees stay green all year.
fact: «Coniferous forest» means a forest made mainly of these trees.
fact: «Deciduous» trees have broad leaves that fall in autumn.
exercise: «The coniferous trees stayed green all winter.» What does coniferous describe? | Flowers that grow in spring | *Trees with cones and needle-like leaves | Trees with broad leaves that fall in autumn | Animals that live in the snow
exercise: «We walked through a coniferous forest of pine and fir.» Find and copy one word that names a coniferous tree. | through | forest | *pine | walked
exercise: Ruby says a coniferous tree loses all its needles every autumn. Is that right? | Only in the snow | Yes, that is what coniferous means | *No, most coniferous trees stay green all year | It depends on the weather alone
test: «Coniferous» and «deciduous» are opposites. What is the difference? | *Coniferous trees have cones and mostly stay green; deciduous trees have broad leaves that fall in autumn | Coniferous trees have broad leaves; deciduous trees have cones | Both kinds of tree lose their leaves in autumn | Both kinds of tree have cones and stay green
test: «The taiga is a huge coniferous forest in the far north.» Which word tells you the forest is mainly made of cone-bearing trees? | Far | North | Huge | *Coniferous
exam: Which of these is NOT a coniferous tree? | Pine | Fir | Spruce | *Oak
